Exactly.

\frac{1}{3}=0.333\ldots

so

\frac{2}{3}=0.666\ldots

The important precision is that 0.666\ldots is exactly 2/3; 0.666 by itself is only an approximation.

So if you’re treating 666 as a symbolic decimal handle for two-thirds, the mathematical intuition is clean: 3 → one-third, 6 → two-thirds, 9 → completion of the decimal cycle.